{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ur3jR35ri5mdwSHjBFhfz9","type":"tool_result","content":"1600\t        \"inclusive a prosa da mensagem de commit (as linhas `printf`). O gerador só \"\n1601\t        \"confere nela os literais de versão, hex e SRI; uma frase verdadeira apenas \"\n1602\t        \"para o re-pin do molde passa inalterada. Leia a mensagem de commit do \"\n1603\t        \"script contra ESTE re-pin antes de assinar.\")\n1604\t    for flag in ctx.get(\"inherited_flags\") or []:\n1605\t        lines += [\"\"] + _wrap(\"Contradição detectada nesta geração: \" + flag + \".\")\n1606\t    return lines\n1607\t\n1608\t\n1609\tdef render_readme(parts: Dict[str, Any], ctx: Dict[str, Any], files: List[str]) -> str:\n1610\t    \"\"\"The pack's README: provenance, the measured values and the files.\"\"\"\n1611\t    rng = (f\"`<{ctx['old_upper']}` → `<{ctx['new_upper']}` (inferior inalterado em \"\n1612\t           f\"`>={ctx['lower']}`)\" if ctx[\"widened\"] else f\"inalterado (`{ctx['new_range']}`)\")\n1613\t    lines = [\n1614\t        f\"# {ctx['pack_name']} — re-pin do Codex CLI {ctx['from_version']} → \"\n1615\t        f\"{ctx['version']} ({ctx['plan_id']})\",\n1616\t        \"\",\n1617\t        f\"Gerado por `{GENERATOR}` em {ctx['date']} a partir do molde `{ctx['mold_rel']}`\",\n1618\t        f\"(sha256 `{ctx['mold_sha']}`). Não edite à mão: regenere o pack.\",\n1619\t        \"\",\n1620\t        \"| valor | medido |\",\n1621\t        \"|---|---|\",\n1622\t        f\"| versão | `{ctx['version']}` (publicada em {ctx['published_date']}) |\",\n1623\t        f\"| range | {rng} |\",\n1624\t        f\"| `npm_integrity` (plataforma `{ctx['platform_spec']}`) | `{ctx['integrity']}` |\",\n1625\t        f\"| `sha256` do payload `{ctx['triple']}` | `{ctx['sha256']}` |\",\n1626\t        f\"| `sha256` dos canônicos vivos (pin, manifesto) | `{ctx['base_pin_sha256']}`, \"\n1627\t        f\"`{ctx['base_man_sha256']}` |\",\n1628\t        f\"| `sha256` dos `.new` (pin, manifesto) | `{ctx['src_pin_sha256']}`, \"\n1629\t        f\"`{ctx['src_man_sha256']}` |\",\n1630\t        f\"| tag que o re-pin segue | `{ctx['ga_tag']}` |\",\n1631\t        \"\",\n1632\t        \"Arquivos: \" + \", \".join(f\"`{f}`\" for f in files) + \".\",\n1633\t        \"\",\n1634\t        f\"O `{ctx['script_name']}` recusa a execução real enquanto houver `{TODO_MARK}` \"\n1635\t        \"no sentinel ou no\",\n1636\t        f\"`{PIN_OUT}`. Os dois `.new` são conferidos por sha256 (`SRC_PIN_SHA256`,\",\n1637\t        \"`SRC_MAN_SHA256`): editar um deles à mão faz o script recusar. Para escrever a\",\n1638\t        \"justificativa no pin, regenere o pack (num diretório novo, ou depois de\",\n1639\t        \"removê-lo) com `--pin-note <arquivo>`.\",\n1640\t    ]\n1641\t    if parts.get(\"rehearsal\") is not None:\n1642\t        lines += [\"\"] + _wrap(_rehearsal_order_note(ctx))\n1643\t    notes = _inherited_prose_notes(parts, ctx)\n1644\t    if notes:\n1645\t        lines += [\"\"] + notes\n1646\t    if parts.get(\"mold_readme\"):\n1647\t        lines += [\"\", \"O que cada passo e cada guard da cerimônia conferem, e por quê: o README \"\n1648\t                  f\"do pack do molde, `{posixpath.dirname(ctx['mold_rel'])}/README.md` (o \"\n1649\t                  \"corpo do script é o do molde).\"]\n1650\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n1651\t\n1652\t\n1653\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1654\t# Rendering of the pin paragraph, the manifest and the sentinel draft\n1655\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1656\t\n1657\t\n1658\tdef render_manifest(old: Dict[str, Any], ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n1659\t    entry_path = old[\"payloads\"][ctx[\"triple\"]][\"path\"]\n1660\t    new = {\n1661\t        \"schema\": 1,\n1662\t        \"package_version\": ctx[\"version\"],\n1663\t        \"npm_integrity\": ctx[\"integrity\"],\n1664\t        \"payloads\": {ctx[\"triple\"]: {\"path\": entry_path, \"sha256\": ctx[\"sha256\"]}},\n1665\t    }\n1666\t    return json.dumps(new, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n1667\t\n1668\t\n1669\tdef render_pin(prefix: List[str], ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n1670\t    \"\"\"The live pin's lines before the range, unchanged, then a blank line\n1671\t    (unless they already end in one), the dated paragraph and the range.\"\"\"\n1672\t    lines = list(prefix)\n1673\t    if lines and lines[-1].strip():\n1674\t        lines.append(\"\")\n1675\t    if ctx[\"widened\"]:\n1676\t        rng = (f\"Upper bound widened <{ctx['old_upper']} -> <{ctx['new_upper']}; \"\n1677\t               f\"LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >={ctx['lower']} (widen-upper-only).\")\n1678\t    else:\n1679\t        rng = (f\"Range UNCHANGED ({ctx['new_range']}): {ctx['version']} already \"\n1680\t               \"sits inside it.\")\n1681\t    para = (f\"re-pin update ({ctx['date']}, pack {ctx['pack_name']}; generated by \"\n1682\t            f\"{GENERATOR}): package_version {ctx['from_version']} -> \"\n1683\t            f\"{ctx['version']}. {rng} The payload manifest is re-pinned in this \"\n1684\t            f\"same pack: payload sha256 {ctx['sha256'][:8]}... for \"\n1685\t            f\"{ctx['version']}/{ctx['triple']}, npm_integrity from the PLATFORM \"\n1686\t            f\"artifact {ctx['platform_spec']} (ADR-182 §5 step 2).\")\n1687\t    lines += _wrap_comment(para)\n1688\t    note = ctx.get(\"pin_note\")\n1689\t    if note:\n1690\t        for paragraph in note:\n1691\t            lines += _wrap_comment(paragraph)\n1692\t    else:\n1693\t        lines += _wrap_comment(\n1694\t            f\"{TODO_MARK}: why this re-pin now; whether it runs outside any open \"\n1695\t            \"release window; whether ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol asks for a \"\n1696\t            \"Phase 4-bis re-run; and the declared consequence (rail measurements \"\n1697\t            \"taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable).\")\n1698\t    lines.append(ctx[\"new_range\"])\n1699\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n1700\t\n1701\t\n1702\tdef read_pin_note(path: str) -> List[str]:\n1703\t    \"\"\"``--pin-note``: the Owner's rationale, as paragraphs (split on blank\n1704\t    lines, each re-wrapped as ``# `` comment lines by ``render_pin``).\"\"\"\n1705\t    try:\n1706\t        raw = Path(path).read_bytes()\n1707\t    except OSError as exc:\n1708\t        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, f\"--pin-note unreadable ({type(exc).__name__})\") from None\n1709\t    text = _mold_text(raw, \"--pin-note\")\n1710\t    if TODO_MARK in text:\n1711\t        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, f\"--pin-note still carries {TODO_MARK}\")\n1712\t    paragraphs = [\" \".join(p.split()) for p in re.split(r\"\\n[ \\t]*\\n\", text)]\n1713\t    paragraphs = [p for p in paragraphs if p]\n1714\t    if not paragraphs:\n1715\t        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, \"--pin-note is empty\")\n1716\t    if any(not c.isprintable() for p in paragraphs for c in p):\n1717\t        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, \"--pin-note carries a control character\")\n1718\t    return paragraphs\n1719\t\n1720\t\n1721\tdef _sentinel_data_line(ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n1722\t    \"\"\"The sentinel's ``Data:`` header line.\n1723\t\n1724\t    A constants-block mold's step 1 rewrites BOTH ``Anchor-SHA:`` and\n1725\t    ``Data:`` with the signing day, and its rehearsal (copied verbatim into\n1726\t    the pack) requires exactly those two lines to change in the ceremony\n1727\t    commit (4 delta lines). A ``Data:`` already equal to the signing day\n1728\t    would change nothing and a same-day rehearsal would go red, so there\n1729\t    the line is a PLACEHOLDER, never the generation date. A heredoc-grammar\n1730\t    mold's step 1 rewrites only ``Anchor-SHA:``; there the line keeps the\n1731\t    generation date, as the hand-built sentinel of that grammar did.\n1732\t    \"\"\"\n1733\t    if ctx[\"grammar\"] == GRAMMAR_CONSTANTS:\n1734\t        return \"Data: (preenchida pelo passo 1 do script de cerimônia)\"\n1735\t    return f\"Data: {ctx['date']}\"\n1736\t\n1737\t\n1738\tdef render_sentinel(ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n1739\t    # justified: one literal template; splitting it would scatter the\n1740\t    # sentinel's section order across helpers.\n1741\t    source =(\"fornecido por --offline-from (não baixado nesta execução)\"\n1742\t              if ctx[\"offline\"] else \"baixado com npm pack num diretório temporário\")\n1743\t    published = ctx[\"published\"] or \"ausente no documento do registry\"\n1744\t    rng = (f\"`<{ctx['old_upper']}` → `<{ctx['new_upper']}` (limite inferior \"\n1745\t           f\"INALTERADO em `>={ctx['lower']}`)\" if ctx[\"widened\"]\n1746\t           else f\"range INALTERADO (`{ctx['new_range']}`)\")\n1747\t    tgz, member = ctx[\"tarball_name\"], ctx[\"member\"]\n1748\t    reg = \" \".join(NPM_REGISTRY_ARGS)\n1749\t    url = ctx[\"tarball_url\"] or \"ausente ou fora do formato https://…/*.tgz\"\n1750\t    return \"\\n\".join([\n1751\t        f\"# {ctx['sentinel_stem']} — sentinel do re-pin do codex CLI \"\n1752\t        f\"{ctx['from_version']} → {ctx['version']}\",\n1753\t        \"\",\n1754\t        f\"Plan: {ctx['plan_id']}\",\n1755\t        f\"Wave: re-pin codex-cli {ctx['from_version']} → {ctx['version']}\",\n1756\t        \"Anchor-SHA: (preenchido pelo passo 1 do script de cerimônia)\",\n1757\t        _sentinel_data_line(ctx),\n1758\t        \"\",\n1759\t        \"## Ratificação\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e0cc364-80e9-432f-8fee-77cee84da142","uuid":"5b51412d-cc66-445c-9373-19147a49e004","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:46:10.689Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py","content":"        \"inclusive a prosa da mensagem de commit (as linhas `printf`). O gerador só \"\n        \"confere nela os literais de versão, hex e SRI; uma frase verdadeira apenas \"\n        \"para o re-pin do molde passa inalterada. Leia a mensagem de commit do \"\n        \"script contra ESTE re-pin antes de assinar.\")\n    for flag in ctx.get(\"inherited_flags\") or []:\n        lines += [\"\"] + _wrap(\"Contradição detectada nesta geração: \" + flag + \".\")\n    return lines\n\n\ndef render_readme(parts: Dict[str, Any], ctx: Dict[str, Any], files: List[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The pack's README: provenance, the measured values and the files.\"\"\"\n    rng = (f\"`<{ctx['old_upper']}` → `<{ctx['new_upper']}` (inferior inalterado em \"\n           f\"`>={ctx['lower']}`)\" if ctx[\"widened\"] else f\"inalterado (`{ctx['new_range']}`)\")\n    lines = [\n        f\"# {ctx['pack_name']} — re-pin do Codex CLI {ctx['from_version']} → \"\n        f\"{ctx['version']} ({ctx['plan_id']})\",\n        \"\",\n        f\"Gerado por `{GENERATOR}` em {ctx['date']} a partir do molde `{ctx['mold_rel']}`\",\n        f\"(sha256 `{ctx['mold_sha']}`). Não edite à mão: regenere o pack.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"| valor | medido |\",\n        \"|---|---|\",\n        f\"| versão | `{ctx['version']}` (publicada em {ctx['published_date']}) |\",\n        f\"| range | {rng} |\",\n        f\"| `npm_integrity` (plataforma `{ctx['platform_spec']}`) | `{ctx['integrity']}` |\",\n        f\"| `sha256` do payload `{ctx['triple']}` | `{ctx['sha256']}` |\",\n        f\"| `sha256` dos canônicos vivos (pin, manifesto) | `{ctx['base_pin_sha256']}`, \"\n        f\"`{ctx['base_man_sha256']}` |\",\n        f\"| `sha256` dos `.new` (pin, manifesto) | `{ctx['src_pin_sha256']}`, \"\n        f\"`{ctx['src_man_sha256']}` |\",\n        f\"| tag que o re-pin segue | `{ctx['ga_tag']}` |\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Arquivos: \" + \", \".join(f\"`{f}`\" for f in files) + \".\",\n        \"\",\n        f\"O `{ctx['script_name']}` recusa a execução real enquanto houver `{TODO_MARK}` \"\n        \"no sentinel ou no\",\n        f\"`{PIN_OUT}`. Os dois `.new` são conferidos por sha256 (`SRC_PIN_SHA256`,\",\n        \"`SRC_MAN_SHA256`): editar um deles à mão faz o script recusar. Para escrever a\",\n        \"justificativa no pin, regenere o pack (num diretório novo, ou depois de\",\n        \"removê-lo) com `--pin-note <arquivo>`.\",\n    ]\n    if parts.get(\"rehearsal\") is not None:\n        lines += [\"\"] + _wrap(_rehearsal_order_note(ctx))\n    notes = _inherited_prose_notes(parts, ctx)\n    if notes:\n        lines += [\"\"] + notes\n    if parts.get(\"mold_readme\"):\n        lines += [\"\", \"O que cada passo e cada guard da cerimônia conferem, e por quê: o README \"\n                  f\"do pack do molde, `{posixpath.dirname(ctx['mold_rel'])}/README.md` (o \"\n                  \"corpo do script é o do molde).\"]\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Rendering of the pin paragraph, the manifest and the sentinel draft\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef render_manifest(old: Dict[str, Any], ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    entry_path = old[\"payloads\"][ctx[\"triple\"]][\"path\"]\n    new = {\n        \"schema\": 1,\n        \"package_version\": ctx[\"version\"],\n        \"npm_integrity\": ctx[\"integrity\"],\n        \"payloads\": {ctx[\"triple\"]: {\"path\": entry_path, \"sha256\": ctx[\"sha256\"]}},\n    }\n    return json.dumps(new, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef render_pin(prefix: List[str], ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The live pin's lines before the range, unchanged, then a blank line\n    (unless they already end in one), the dated paragraph and the range.\"\"\"\n    lines = list(prefix)\n    if lines and lines[-1].strip():\n        lines.append(\"\")\n    if ctx[\"widened\"]:\n        rng = (f\"Upper bound widened <{ctx['old_upper']} -> <{ctx['new_upper']}; \"\n               f\"LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >={ctx['lower']} (widen-upper-only).\")\n    else:\n        rng = (f\"Range UNCHANGED ({ctx['new_range']}): {ctx['version']} already \"\n               \"sits inside it.\")\n    para = (f\"re-pin update ({ctx['date']}, pack {ctx['pack_name']}; generated by \"\n            f\"{GENERATOR}): package_version {ctx['from_version']} -> \"\n            f\"{ctx['version']}. {rng} The payload manifest is re-pinned in this \"\n            f\"same pack: payload sha256 {ctx['sha256'][:8]}... for \"\n            f\"{ctx['version']}/{ctx['triple']}, npm_integrity from the PLATFORM \"\n            f\"artifact {ctx['platform_spec']} (ADR-182 §5 step 2).\")\n    lines += _wrap_comment(para)\n    note = ctx.get(\"pin_note\")\n    if note:\n        for paragraph in note:\n            lines += _wrap_comment(paragraph)\n    else:\n        lines += _wrap_comment(\n            f\"{TODO_MARK}: why this re-pin now; whether it runs outside any open \"\n            \"release window; whether ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol asks for a \"\n            \"Phase 4-bis re-run; and the declared consequence (rail measurements \"\n            \"taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable).\")\n    lines.append(ctx[\"new_range\"])\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef read_pin_note(path: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"``--pin-note``: the Owner's rationale, as paragraphs (split on blank\n    lines, each re-wrapped as ``# `` comment lines by ``render_pin``).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        raw = Path(path).read_bytes()\n    except OSError as exc:\n        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, f\"--pin-note unreadable ({type(exc).__name__})\") from None\n    text = _mold_text(raw, \"--pin-note\")\n    if TODO_MARK in text:\n        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, f\"--pin-note still carries {TODO_MARK}\")\n    paragraphs = [\" \".join(p.split()) for p in re.split(r\"\\n[ \\t]*\\n\", text)]\n    paragraphs = [p for p in paragraphs if p]\n    if not paragraphs:\n        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, \"--pin-note is empty\")\n    if any(not c.isprintable() for p in paragraphs for c in p):\n        raise RePinError(EXIT_INPUT, \"--pin-note carries a control character\")\n    return paragraphs\n\n\ndef _sentinel_data_line(ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The sentinel's ``Data:`` header line.\n\n    A constants-block mold's step 1 rewrites BOTH ``Anchor-SHA:`` and\n    ``Data:`` with the signing day, and its rehearsal (copied verbatim into\n    the pack) requires exactly those two lines to change in the ceremony\n    commit (4 delta lines). A ``Data:`` already equal to the signing day\n    would change nothing and a same-day rehearsal would go red, so there\n    the line is a PLACEHOLDER, never the generation date. A heredoc-grammar\n    mold's step 1 rewrites only ``Anchor-SHA:``; there the line keeps the\n    generation date, as the hand-built sentinel of that grammar did.\n    \"\"\"\n    if ctx[\"grammar\"] == GRAMMAR_CONSTANTS:\n        return \"Data: (preenchida pelo passo 1 do script de cerimônia)\"\n    return f\"Data: {ctx['date']}\"\n\n\ndef render_sentinel(ctx: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    # justified: one literal template; splitting it would scatter the\n    # sentinel's section order across helpers.\n    source =(\"fornecido por --offline-from (não baixado nesta execução)\"\n              if ctx[\"offline\"] else \"baixado com npm pack num diretório temporário\")\n    published = ctx[\"published\"] or \"ausente no documento do registry\"\n    rng = (f\"`<{ctx['old_upper']}` → `<{ctx['new_upper']}` (limite inferior \"\n           f\"INALTERADO em `>={ctx['lower']}`)\" if ctx[\"widened\"]\n           else f\"range INALTERADO (`{ctx['new_range']}`)\")\n    tgz, member = ctx[\"tarball_name\"], ctx[\"member\"]\n    reg = \" \".join(NPM_REGISTRY_ARGS)\n    url = ctx[\"tarball_url\"] or \"ausente ou fora do formato https://…/*.tgz\"\n    return \"\\n\".join([\n        f\"# {ctx['sentinel_stem']} — sentinel do re-pin do codex CLI \"\n        f\"{ctx['from_version']} → {ctx['version']}\",\n        \"\",\n        f\"Plan: {ctx['plan_id']}\",\n        f\"Wave: re-pin codex-cli {ctx['from_version']} → {ctx['version']}\",\n        \"Anchor-SHA: (preenchido pelo passo 1 do script de cerimônia)\",\n        _sentinel_data_line(ctx),\n        \"\",\n        \"## Ratificação\",","numLines":160,"startLine":1600,"totalLines":2314}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ur3jR35ri5mdwSHjBFhfz9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
