liberately canonical-only. Condition 5 is not affected.\n  - The NF-04 ast oracle now parses toggles.py (tests/test_night_mode.py:1728, :1846), so the docstring's claim still holds.\n  - install.sh copies each top-level _lib entry, new packages included (install.sh:1520-1547).\n- profile-opus-4-7:\n  - latency.py has the same logic as the removed run_hook_latency (only comments trimmed).\n  - _REF_EXEC_SOURCE (reference.py:130-228) is byte-identical, so ref_source_sha256 does not change. The constants and the exit-code contract (phase 1 / phase 2) are the same.\n  - The docstring is restored from hook_latency_docs.\n- reality-ledger:\n  - __all__ is complete in all ten part modules.\n  - `from .constants import *` supplies the default values the functions need when they are defined.\n  - _REPO_ROOT, redact_secrets and the itimer guard come from the facade.\n  - The self-exclusion gains '/_reality_ledger_parts/' (constants.py:55), which keeps the anti-self-referential rule.\n  - _read_known_actions handles the audit_emit split by parsing files only, never importing them (audit_actions.py:38-114).\n  - The tool stays advisory-only.\n- re-pin-codex:\n  - The guard now reads literal paths, checked by _GUARD_PATH_RE before rendering (re-pin-codex.py:956-964) and passed after `--`, so they cannot be quoted or injected.\n  - A grep exit code of 2 or more now dies. The old guard treated an unreadable or missing file as clean, so this is strictly more fail-closed.\n  - The legacy guard is still accepted (:944-952, :1346-1356).\n  - _check_guard_read_files runs before anything is written.\n  - _repin_guard.py reaches installs through the *.py glob (install.sh:1606-1611), as CHANGELOG lines 342-346 say.\n- Python: everything new is standard-library only and Python 3.9 compatible (FunctionType rebinding, re.escape, typing).\n- Conditions: condition 7 holds for these three facades. Condition 10 is not contradicted. No declared condition is false in this payload.\n\nFINDINGS\nP2-1 re-pin-codex.py:496-497 and :2171-2172 — the generator mislabels the change it makes to the Codex pin range.\n- Scenario:\n  - The live pin's range is the unbounded floor `>=0.128.0` (.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt:199; CHANGELOG 199-201).\n  - The next pack generated against it gets plan_range(upper=None), which returns `>=0.128.0,<X.(Y+1).0` with widened=True.\n  - run() then sets old_upper equal to new_upper.\n  - The pin paragraph (:1675-1677), the sentinel (:1744-1746), the README (:1611) and the commit message (:1437-1439) all say \"Upper bound widened <0.161.0 -> <0.161.0 … (widen-upper-only)\".\n  - Applying the pack actually adds an upper bound to an unbounded floor. That narrows the policy and reverses the version-floor route (condition 10; CHANGELOG 447-450), while the signed text calls it a widening.\n  - OLD_UPPER is invented. The rehearsal, copied word for word from the newest mold, asserts `live_pin[-1] == f\">={lower},<{old_up}\"` (PLAN-194/codex-pin-0160/rehearse-pin-0160.sh:267), so it fails.\n  - The docstring at :55-56 (\"widened upper-only, and only when the version falls outside it\") is no longer true.\n- Why P2: the tool is maintainer-only (it refuses in installs), the failure is closed (newer CLIs get refused) and the rehearsal catches it.\n- Minimal fix: when upper is None, either refuse by name (\"live pin is an unbounded floor; the bounded pack grammar cannot express it\") or render the change honestly (\"upper bound ADDED: none -> <X\", with no fabricated OLD_UPPER and widened=False). Add a plan_range test with upper=None.\n\nP2-2 night-mode.py:327-331 — a relocated copy now crashes instead of being refused as documented.\n- Scenario:\n  - _lib._night_mode_parts is now imported when the module loads, before main() runs _check_self_path().\n  - Take a relocated copy whose parents[2] has no .claude/hooks/_lib/_night_mode_parts, such as .claude/nm.py or a copy outside any repo.\n  - It now dies with an ImportError traceback and exit