oes not change. The constants and the exit-code contract (phase 1 / phase 2) are the same.\\n  - The docstring is restored from hook_latency_docs.\\n- reality-ledger:\\n  - __all__ is complete in all ten part modules.\\n  - `from .constants import *` supplies the default values the functions need when they are defined.\\n  - _REPO_ROOT, redact_secrets and the itimer guard come from the facade.\\n  - The self-exclusion gains '/_reality_ledger_parts/' (constants.py:55), which keeps the anti-self-referential rule.\\n  - _read_known_actions handles the audit_emit split by parsing files only, never importing them (audit_actions.py:38-114).\\n  - The tool stays advisory-only.\\n- re-pin-codex:\\n  - The guard now reads literal paths, checked by _GUARD_PATH_RE before rendering (re-pin-codex.py:956-964) and passed after `--`, so they cannot be quoted or injected.\\n  - A grep exit code of 2 or more now dies. The old guard treated an unreadable or missing file as clean, so this is strictly more fail-closed.\\n  - The legacy guard is still accepted (:944-952, :1346-1356).\\n  - _check_guard_read_files runs before anything is written.\\n  - _repin_guard.py reaches installs through the *.py glob (install.sh:1606-1611), as CHANGELOG lines 342-346 say.\\n- Python: everything new is standard-library only and Python 3.9 compatible (FunctionType rebinding, re.escape, typing).\\n- Conditions: condition 7 holds for these three facades. Condition 10 is not contradicted. No declared condition is false in this payload.\\n\\nFINDINGS\\nP2-1 re-pin-codex.py:496-497 and :2171-2172 — the generator mislabels the change it makes to the Codex pin range.\\n- Scenario:\\n  - The live pin's range is the unbounded floor `>=0.128.0` (.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt:199; CHANGELOG 199-201).\\n  - The next pack generated against it gets plan_range(upper=None), which returns `>=0.128.0,<X.(Y+1).0` with widened=True.\\n  - run() then sets old_upper equal to new_upper.\\n  - The pin paragraph (:1675-1677), the sentinel (:1744-1746), the README (:1611) and the commit message (:1437-1439) all say \\\"Upper bound widened <0.161.0 -> <0.161.0 … (widen-upper-only)\\\".\\n  - Applying the pack actually adds an upper bound to an unbounded floor. That narrows the policy and reverses the version-floor route (condition 10; CHANGELOG 447-450), while the signed text calls it a widening.\\n  - OLD_UPPER is invented. The rehearsal, copied word for word from the newest mold, asserts `live_pin[-1] == f\\\">={lower},<{old_up}\\\"` (PLAN-194/codex-pin-0160/rehearse-pin-0160.sh:267), so it fails.\\n  - The docstring at :55-56 (\\\"widened upper-only, and only when the version falls outside it\\\") is no longer true.\\n- Why P2: the tool is maintainer-only (it refuses in installs), the failure is closed (newer CLIs get refused) and the rehearsal catches it.\\n- Minimal fix: when upper is None, either refuse by name (\\\"live pin is an unbounded floor; the bounded pack grammar cannot express it\\\") or render the change honestly (\\\"upper bound ADDED: none -> <X\\\", with no fabricated OLD_UPPER and widened=False). Add a plan_range test with upper=None.\\n\\nP2-2 night-mode.py:327-331 — a relocated copy now crashes instead of being refused as documented.\\n- Scenario:\\n  - _lib._night_mode_parts is now imported when the module loads, before main() runs _check_self_path().\\n  - Take a relocated copy whose parents[2] has no .claude/hooks/_lib/_night_mode_parts, such as .claude/nm.py or a copy outside any repo.\\n  - It now dies with an ImportError traceback and exit code 1, instead of the NF-08b refusal (exit 2 plus a `night-mode-event … result=refused` line).\\n  - Nothing is written, so this still fails closed. But the docstring's exit-code table (night-mode.py:204-211) is wrong for this case.\\n- Minimal fix: wrap the import in try/except ImportError, print a diagnostic to stderr and exit 2. Or amend the docstring.\\n\\nP2-3 (observation; not a new class) _lib/_night_mode_parts/toggles.py — the posture-write functions are reachable under a new name.\\n- Scenario:\\n  - cmd_on, cmd_off and cmd_off_discard_snapshot can now be reached by the module name _lib._night_mode_parts.\\n  - The _e4 matcher does not key on that name (_E4_POSTURE_TOGGLE_SCRIPTS, _bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:376).\\n  - The NF-08b self-path check lives only in the facade's main(), so this route skips it.\\n  - This is not a new class: arbitrary `python3 -c` could already load night-mode.py through importlib with an obfuscated path and call cmd_on. The files are canonical-tier.\\n- Minimal fix (optional): note the package in the matcher's comment or coherence set, or run the self-path check at the entry of cmd_on and cmd_off.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\\nNone. I found no P1 in this payload.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\nP2-1, P2-2 and P2-3 above.\"}","structured_output":{"decision":"GO","sentence":"No declared condition is false against this payload's code and there is no P0; the three facade moves behave the same as before, the re-pin guard now refuses more cases, and the only defects are P2 follow-ups in the maintainer-only re-pin generator and in night-mode's exit-code documentation.","report":"PAYLOAD 31/32 covers four files: .claude/scripts/night-mode.py, profile-opus-4-7.py, re-pin-codex.py and reality-ledger.py. I also read the new code they depend on in the candidate tree: _lib/_night_mode_parts/, _lib/_profile_opus_parts/, _lib/_reality_ledger_parts/ and .claude/scripts/_repin_guard.py.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED (no finding)\n- night-mode (moved code, item 4):\n  - helpers.py and toggles.py repeat the removed body line for line.\n  - install() (_night_mode_parts/__init__.py:14-31) rebuilds each function with the facade's globals. Every free name still resolves:\n    - from the facade: REPO_ROOT, NIGHT_MODE, MARKER_VERSION, _RESTORABLE_MODES, _DISCARD_HINT, _TEST_SEAM_ENV, _CANONICAL_SELF_PARTS, _INVOKED_SELF and the standard-library imports;\n    - from helpers' __all__: the module constants _LINE_BREAKS, _ONE_LINE_TABLE and _SUMMARY_TOKEN_SAFE.\n  - Behaviour is unchanged on these points:\n    - fail-closed handling of the marker and the overlay;\n    - the CI refusal;\n    - the NF-08b self-path check, still in main() before dispatch (night-mode.py:518-533);\n    - the order of writes (settings, then marker);\n    - the summary and audit records written as a pair.\n  - Protection tier is unchanged:\n    - .claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py is canonical (canonical_edit/guards.py:34), the same tier as .claude/scripts/night-mode.py (guards.py:235).\n    - check_arbitration_kernel.py:274-276 says the writer is deliberately canonical-only. Condition 5 is not affected.\n  - The NF-04 ast oracle now parses toggles.py (tests/test_night_mode.py:1728, :1846), so the docstring's claim still holds.\n  - install.sh copies each top-level _lib entry, new packages included (install.sh:1520-1547).\n- profile-opus-4-7:\n  - latency.py has the same logic as the removed run_hook_latency (only comments trimmed).\n  - _REF_EXEC_SOURCE (reference.py:130-228) is byte-identical, so ref_source_sha256 does not change. The constants and the exit-code contract (phase 1 / phase 2) are the same.\n  - The docstring is restored from hook_latency_docs.\n- reality-ledger:\n  - __all__ is complete in all ten part modules.\n  - `from .constants import *` supplies the default values the functions need when they are defined.\n  - _REPO_ROOT, redact_secrets and the itimer guard come from the facade.\n  - The self-exclusion gains '/_reality_ledger_parts/' (constants.py:55), which keeps the anti-self-referential rule.\n  - _read_known_actions handles the audit_emit split by parsing files only, never importing them (audit_actions.py:38-114).\n  - The tool stays advisory-only.\n- re-pin-codex:\n  - The guard now reads literal paths, checked by _GUARD_PATH_RE before rendering (re-pin-codex.py:956-964) and passed after `--`, so they cannot be quoted or injected.\n  - A grep exit code of 2 or more now dies. The old guard treated an unreadable or missing file as clean, so this is strictly more fail-closed.\n  - The legacy guard is still accepted (:944-952, :1346-1356).\n  - _check_guard_read_files runs before anything is written.\n  - _repin_guard.py reaches installs through the *.py glob (install.sh:1606-1611), as CHANGELOG lines 342-346 say.\n- Python: everything new is standard-library only and Python 3.9 compatible (FunctionType rebinding, re.escape, typing).\n- Conditions: condition 7 holds for these three facades. Condition 10 is not contradicted. No declared condition is false in this payload.\n\nFINDINGS\nP2-1 re-pin-codex.py:496-497 and :2171-2172 — the generator mislabels the change it makes to the Codex pin range.\n- Scenario:\n  - The live pin's range is the unbounded floor `>=0.128.0` (.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt:199; CHANGELOG 199-201).\n  - The next pack generated against it gets plan_range(upper=None), which returns `>=0.128.0,<X.(Y+1).0` with widened=True.\n  - run() then sets old_upper equal to new_upper.\n  - The pin paragraph (:1675-1677), the sentinel (:1744-1746), the README (:1611) and the commit message (:1437-1439) all say \"Upper bound widened <0.161.0 -> <0.161.0 … (widen-upper-only)\".\n  - Applying the pack actually adds an upper bound to an unbounded floor. That narrows the policy and reverses the version-floor route (condition 10; CHANGELOG 447-450), while the signed text calls it a widening.\n  - OLD_UPPER is invented. The rehearsal, copied word for word from the newest mold, asserts `live_pin[-1] == f\">={lower},<{old_up}\"` (PLAN-194/codex-pin-0160/rehearse-pin-0160.sh:267), so it fails.\n  - The docstring at :55-56 (\"widened upper-only, and only when the version falls outside it\") is no longer true.\n- Why P2: the tool is maintainer-only (it refuses in installs), the failure is closed (newer CLIs get refused) and the rehearsal catches it.\n- Minimal fix: when upper is None, either refuse by name (\"live pin is an unbounded floor; the bounded pack grammar cannot express it\") or render the change honestly (\"upper bound ADDED: none -> <X\", with no fabricated OLD_UPPER and widened=False). Add a plan_range test with upper=None.\n\nP2-2 night-mode.py:327-331 — a relocated copy now crashes instead of being refused as documented.\n- Scenario:\n  - _lib._night_mode_parts is now imported when the module loads, before main() runs _check_self_path().\n  - Take a relocated copy whose parents[2] has no .claude/hooks/_lib/_night_mode_parts, such as .claude/nm.py or a copy outside any repo.\n  - It now dies with an ImportError traceback and exit code 1, instead of the NF-08b refusal (exit 2 plus a `night-mode-event … result=refused` line).\n  - Nothing is written, so this still fails closed. But the docstring's exit-code table (night-mode.py:204-211) is wrong for this case.\n- Minimal fix: wrap the import in try/except ImportError, print a diagnostic to stderr and exit 2. Or amend the docstring.\n\nP2-3 (observation; not a new class) _lib/_night_mode_parts/toggles.py — the posture-write functions are reachable under a new name.\n- Scenario:\n  - cmd_on, cmd_off and cmd_off_discard_snapshot can now be reached by the module name _lib._night_mode_parts.\n  - The _e4 matcher does not key on that name (_E4_POSTURE_TOGGLE_SCRIPTS, _bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:376).\n  - The NF-08b self-path check lives only in the facade's main(), so this route skips it.\n  - This is not a new class: arbitrary `python3 -c` could already load night-mode.py through importlib with an obfuscated path and call cmd_on. The files are canonical-tier.\n- Minimal fix (optional): note the package in the matcher's comment or coherence set, or run the self-path check at the entry of cmd_on and cmd_off.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone. I found no P1 in this payload.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1, P2-2 and P2-3 above."},"ttft_ms":7144,"type":"result","duration_ms":441295,"uuid":"171d9924-3928-4992-9697-4154ae4